{
  "_comment": "bots-stage1 (docs/progress/bots-stage1.md): optional sidecar read by tools/server/make_base_json.py next to the map descriptor. Positions are navmesh-verified in-game (UiBridge teleports / player positions, 2026-09-19). Radii follow Factory's SpawnSphereParams (bots 25-35 m). Kept out of equator.json so the Unity editor's JsonUtility reader never sees these fields. Only the ground floor is playable on Equator; the upper rings are decoration (user, 2026-09-20), so no spawn goes above y 0.2 (the former ring2-west point at y 10.8 was a NavMesh island). bots-stage3 (2026-09-20): PMCs come from BossLocationSpawn entries (BossName pmcUSEC/pmcBEAR), not from waves — Factory ships four such entries; SPT's PmcWaveGenerator only replaces them for maps listed in pmc.json customPmcWaves, so ours survive untouched. boss_zone names the zone explicitly (BossLocationSpawn.FindZoneWithCorrectName searches every BotZone), and the bot spawns carry the BotPmc category so BotZone.HasPmcBotSpawns is true as well. Equator ArenaMode integration (2026-09-20): two additional bot points at each end preserve the 25 m Arena bot-distance floor with at least three distant candidate points (the injector requests two bots per burst). All four additions passed UiBridge NavMesh, zone, full path and standing-room checks from the atrium and Usec niche on the 10404-vertex/4572-triangle bake. South-east uses the verified snapped point (8.7, 0.1, -28.4). Four other tested candidates were rejected during independent review because they overlapped player spawn coordinates. The extra All player marker gives both PMC sides a southern entry; ArenaMode respawns use all Player markers.",
